WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.988
Then the plan.

2
00:00:00.988 --> 00:00:02.818
Of eleven actions, three write:

3
00:00:02.818 --> 00:00:07.796
a connector's full-control site permission
is removed because its selected-sites

4
00:00:07.796 --> 00:00:12.407
replacement is already granted, the
broad directory permission is removed,

5
00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:16.726
and a partner app's all-users grant
is narrowed to just reading profiles.

6
00:00:16.726 --> 00:00:20.938
The dry run shows the point of the
whole exercise: both removals go

7
00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:25.463
through Microsoft Graph's service
principal, the resource, not the app.

8
00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:30.600
Applying it to the fake sends three writes,
and a hash nobody approved is refused.

9
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.020
Delete the output afterwards,
because the review names real owners.
